			"widgets_values":[
				"A Viking shieldmaiden rides into battle on a muscular black stallion, filmed with dynamic, shaky close-to-mid shots that emphasize raw intensity. She’s clad in a weathered leather tunic dyed deep indigo, layered over chainmail that glints faintly through rips, her hips bound with a thick woolen belt strung with a iron seax (short sword) and a small round shield etched with a raven symbol. Her hair—thick, braided with strands of red wool and tiny bronze beads—whips wild in the wind as she leans low over the horse’s neck, jaw set, eyes blazing with fierce focus.\n\nThe stallion rears briefly, hooves kicking up mud and grass, before charging into a chaotic skirmish: enemy warriors in rusted armor fall back as she swings a double-bladed axe, its edge glistening with rain and blood. Her leather boots grip iron stirrups, one foot lifting to push off as she leans into a strike, her shield arm bracing against a clashing sword.\n\nThe scene is set at dusk, with a storm-darkened sky 撕裂 by cracks of lightning; rain slashes sideways, soaking her hair and clothes, making the ground slick with mud and blood. The soundtrack of clanging metal, the stallion’s snorts, and her guttural battle cries merges with the howl of wind through the nearby fjord cliffs.\n\nHer face, streaked with war paint (crimson and charcoal), is fierce yet determined—no fear, only primal resolve—as she cuts a path through the fray, the horse’s mane matted with sweat, its flanks flecked with foam. Occasional slow-mo shots capture the axe’s arc, the spray of rain off her shield, and the fire in her eyes as she locks gaze with an enemy before striking.\n\nNo softness, no hesitation—just the raw, unbridled fury of a Viking warrior in her element, horse and rider moving as one through the chaos of combat."
			],
